## Context

`deliverables/_shared/_includes/cop-topic-structure.md` carries a four-column
table that does not render as one table. Two defects, both mechanical:

- **Line 38** — the row for "Green bonds, Art. 2.1(c)" ends with an HTML
  comment *after* its closing pipe (`… | 2016--present | <!-- corrected
  2026-07-11 (0244) … -->`). That trailing text is a fifth cell against a
  four-column header, so the row renders with a stray column.
- **Line 42** — the row for "WIM, Santiago Network, L\&D Fund" sits below two
  blank-line-separated comment blocks, so it belongs to no table at all. It
  renders as a paragraph of pipe-separated text, outside the table it was
  written for.

The provenance comments themselves are worth keeping — they record the 0244
verification pass. They just cannot sit inside a table body.

This is a prose file in the manuscript workpackage, so it is filed for the
author rather than edited autonomously.

## Relevant files

- `deliverables/_shared/_includes/cop-topic-structure.md:33-42` — the table
- `tests/test_markdown_table_shape.py` — the parser that found it; it covers
  *generated* tables only, which is why this hand-authored one went unnoticed

## Actions

1. Move both provenance comments out of the table body — above the table, or
   below its last row, with one blank line separating them.
2. Restore the `WIM, Santiago Network, L\&D Fund` row to the table body.
3. Decide whether the 0340 sweep should extend to hand-authored
   `_includes/*.md`. It reads them at no cost; the question is whether a prose
   defect should fail an adherence gate the author does not run.

## Test

Red first:

```python
def test_cop_topic_structure_is_one_table():
    from test_markdown_table_shape import malformed_rows
    text = (REPO_ROOT / "deliverables/_shared/_includes/cop-topic-structure.md").read_text()
    assert not malformed_rows(text)
```

It reports two offenders today (lines 38 and 42) and none after the fix.

## Verification

- [ ] `malformed_rows` returns nothing for the file
- [ ] The rendered PDF shows one eight-row table, no stray column
- [ ] Both 0244 provenance comments survive in the source

## Invariants

- No factual change to any cell — this is a layout repair, not a content edit.
- The corrected EIB/World Bank green-bond attribution from 0244 stays as
  written.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The file parses as a single well-formed table
- [ ] An explicit decision recorded on whether the sweep covers `_includes/`
